<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- This file is deliberately almost empty, and most of that IS the privacy
	     architecture. Read the caveat before reading the list.

	     THE CAVEAT: the App Sandbox is NOT enabled here, because Tier 1 (Accessibility
	     reading window titles of other processes) is incompatible with it. Without the
	     sandbox, an absent entitlement is a statement of intent, not a kernel
	     restriction — an unsandboxed process may open a socket whatever this file says.
	     docs/PRIVACY.md §8.1 states that plainly rather than hiding it, and it was as
	     true before the app had an updater as it is now.

	     Absent, and never to be added:
	       com.apple.security.network.server            nothing here listens, ever, and
	                                                    `make verify` fails if this key
	                                                    ever appears
	       com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
	                                                    not in this file. Scripts/bundle.sh
	                                                    adds it at signing time, and only to
	                                                    a build with no Team ID, because the
	                                                    hardened runtime cannot load the
	                                                    embedded Sparkle without it. The
	                                                    comment there says why that costs
	                                                    nothing
	       com.apple.security.device.camera
	       com.apple.security.device.audio-input        mic STATE is read from CoreAudio
	                                                    without ever opening a stream

	     Absent, and NOT claimed as a guarantee:
	       com.apple.security.network.client            the app does make one outbound
	                                                    request — the update check. This
	                                                    key is not here because without
	                                                    the sandbox it would not be
	                                                    enforcing anything either way. A
	                                                    future sandboxed flavour would
	                                                    need it, and would therefore ship
	                                                    without the updater instead.

	     What actually constrains the network behaviour is checkable and is checked:
	     the app's own binary references no networking symbol, the only network code is
	     Sparkle.framework, the only endpoint is SUFeedURL in Info.plist, and every
	     update is EdDSA-verified before it can install. Run `make verify`. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
